<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Feodor I of Russia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1557–1598</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Fyodor I Ivanovich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Feodor I was tsar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> from 1584 to 1598, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a> and the last of the Rurikid line to rule Muscovy. Pious and withdrawn, he left government to his brother-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boris-godunov">Boris Godunov</a>, under whose regency the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> Patriarchate was established in 1589 and Russia recovered towns on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-finland">Gulf of Finland</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. His death without an heir brought Godunov to the throne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/feodor-i-of-russia.jpg" alt="Feodor I of Russia" width="320" height="446" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shakko · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fedor_ioannovich01_reconstruction.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
